123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Climate variability and the growing occurrence of extreme weather events present critical challenges for environmental assessment and infrastructure resilience worldwide. The ClimateScope project is a comprehensive, data-driven web application developed to analyze, visualize, and interpret large-scale climate data in order to support informed decision-making. The system integrates historical and near real-time weather datasets to examine key climatic parameters, including temperature, humidity, precipitation, wind speed, air quality, and extreme weather indicators across multiple geographical regions.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The project adopts a milestone-based development .methodology encompassing data acquisition and preprocessing, exploratory data analysis, statistical evaluation, and interactive dashboard design. Using Python-based technologies such as Pandas, Plotly, and Streamlit, the application delivers intuitive and interactive visualizations, including time-series trend analyses, geospatial choropleth maps, heatmaps, and extreme event visual analytics. These visual components enable users to identify climate patterns, regional variations, and anomalies effectively.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The application is deployed as a scalable web-based platform on Streamlit Community Cloud, ensuring accessibility, interactivity, and real-time data exploration for researchers, policymakers, and stakeholders.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
